; A defaulted variant key is checked, not only filled in.
;
; No `(anchor :name origin)` here. `(light :kind spot)` selects the
; `spot` variant, `:aim` is omitted, its default `origin` is
; materialized, and the cross-ref lookup over it misses:
;
;   not_cross_ref at [light aim default]
;   form `light` keyword `:aim` default `origin` does not name a
;   `(lights/anchor …)` instance
;
; The path ends in `default`: the value that failed is one the author
; never wrote. The repair is either to declare the anchor the schema
; assumes, or to write an `:aim` that names one that exists. Before
; variant-key defaults reached the overlay this document was silent,
; and the omission was accepted on the strength of a value nothing had
; supplied.
;
;   cat examples/plugins/variant-defaults/plugin.sjon \
;       examples/plugins/variant-defaults/example-missing-anchor.sjon | sjon validate - --no-project

(light :kind spot)
